[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "adr-2608201300-jvm-new-surface-scaffold-guard"
  :adr/title "Scaffold and deps edits must not grow jvm-runtime-deps or production .clj"
  :adr/status "accepted"
  :adr/date "2026-08-20"
  :adr/related ["adr-2608170200-jvm-dependency-surface-measured-repowide"
                "adr-2608136000-five-questions-before-believing-a-check"]
  :adr/body "Context

`90-docs/migration/kotoba-wasm-runtime-cutover.edn` already sets
`:new-jvm-runtime-dependencies :forbidden`. Detector
`scripts/verify-jvm-dependency-surface.cljs` measures standing
`:jvm-runtime-deps` and `:jvm-source` debt. Neither stops an agent from
scaffolding a new repo with production `.clj` or adding cheshire to
top-level `:deps` — prose in CLAUDE.md and the cutover contract was not
enough (same class as branch-sync: reminder ≠ enforcement).

Decision

1. Admission (new only). Editing an existing production `.clj` or an
   existing third-party leaf is allowed. Creating a new production `.clj`
   path, or adding a new top-level maven/external-git leaf that is not
   `org.clojure/clojure` and not lint/test/build tool coords, is refused.
2. Portable default for scaffold. New project source is `.cljc` / `.cljs`
   / `.kotoba`. `test/` and `*_test.clj` remain allowed. Workspace git and
   `:local/root` deps remain allowed. Tool coords stay under aliases.
3. Enforcement. `scripts/jvm_new_surface_policy.cljs` classifies;
   PreToolUse hook `.claude/hooks/jvm-new-surface-guard.cljs` on
   Write|Edit|StrReplace and on `git commit`/`git push`. Fail-open on
   parse/IO errors. Owner override: `JVM_NEW_SURFACE_ALLOW=1`.
4. Policy home. `manifest/repository-rules.edn` `:workspace-policies
   :jvm-new-surface`. Skill `new-project-scaffold` states the same defaults.

Consequences

Standing debt does not shrink by this ADR. Growth stops. Detector still
reports what already exists. Mass port of legacy `.clj` is out of scope."}]
